h323plus-plugins multi-license notice
=====================================

This repository is a multi-license source distribution. There is no single
license that applies to every file in this repository.

The license notices in each source file are authoritative for that file. When a
file carries its own copyright or license header, keep that header intact and
follow that license.

Complete texts for standard licenses referenced by files in this repository are
provided under the LICENSES/ directory. See LICENSES/README.md for provenance:

- LICENSES/MPL-1.0.txt
- LICENSES/MPL-1.1.txt
- LICENSES/GPL-2.0-or-later.txt
- LICENSES/LGPL-2.1-or-later.txt

Some files contain project-specific or copyright-holder-specific notices that
are not replaced by a standard license text. Those notices remain in the
source-file headers and must be preserved.

Component guidance
------------------

Files that identify the Mozilla Public License Version 1.0 in their source
headers remain distributed under MPL-1.0.

Files without a clear license notice must not be assumed to be covered by
MPL-1.0 or any other repository-wide default license. Their origin and
applicable terms must be determined before redistribution.

Third-party and codec-specific code
-----------------------------------

This repository also includes third-party codec and helper code under other
terms, including but not limited to:

- `H.264/gpl/`: GPL-2.0-or-later helper code.
- `H.264/shared/`, static-link files, and some `common/` files: MPL/GPL
  dual-license notices as specified in each source header.
- `H.263-ffmpeg/`: MPL-1.0 plugin code with FFmpeg/libavcodec/libavformat dependency terms
  applying to linked FFmpeg components.
- `common/vs-stdint.h`: its own BSD-style notice.

See THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md for the component index and attribution details.

Patent and codec terms
----------------------

Some audio/video codec standards may have patent, trademark, export, or
field-of-use obligations outside the source-code copyright license. Review the
codec-specific notices and applicable laws before distributing or deploying
the plugins.

Binary distribution
-------------------

If you distribute built plugin binaries, you are responsible for complying with:

- all source-code license obligations for the files compiled into the binary;
- the licenses of dynamically or statically linked libraries such as FFmpeg,
  libavcodec, libavutil, x264, PTLib, and H.323 Plus;
- any required source availability, notices, and attribution obligations.

For every binary release, complete and retain the record described in
docs/DEPENDENCY-LICENSE-REVIEW.md.

No warranty
-----------

The software is provided as-is, without warranty of any kind, to the extent
permitted by the applicable licenses.
